        "text": "Counter-considerations: upside risk is another transfer or proprietors-income boost, stronger June withholding, or less reversal of May farm payments, which would land above the interval. Downside risk is a sharper relief-payment reversal, weaker bonus/proprietor income, or larger tax-withholding drag, which would land below the interval. Outside the interval would require either a monthly drop larger than about 166 billion from May or a gain above about 248 billion from May."
